        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(trajectory): session.ended timestamp matches model.completed before cleanup",
        "body": "Closes #102014\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where trajectory exports showed `session.ended` with the same timestamp as `model.completed`, so cleanup duration looked like zero even when teardown took real wall-clock time.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`session.ended` was recorded in `finalizeEmbeddedAttempt` immediately after `model.completed`, then marked complete so the cleanup phase skipped it. This PR defers `session.ended` until after resource cleanup, keeps the finalize terminal status/error, and flushes trajectory events before and after cleanup so earlier events stay durable if teardown hangs. No new event types or exporter knobs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators reading trajectory traces can measure real session end time versus model compute time, including cleanup latency.\n\n## Evidence\n\nVerified at HEAD `d371ea1f01` (post rebase). Source ordering before the fix: finalize emits `model.completed` then `session.ended`, then `trajectoryEndRecorded = true`, so cleanup never re-emitted.\n\nFocused tests:\n\n```\npnpm test src/trajectory/runtime.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-session-cleanup.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-execution-settle.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-trajectory-status.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/run/attempt-trajectory-flush-cleanup.test.ts\n\nTest Files  5 passed (5)\n     Tests  37 passed (37)\n```\n\nCI follow-up (`6c4e13c66b`): un-exported unused `AttemptTrajectoryTerminalStatus` so `check-dependencies` Knip no longer flags it. Re-ran focused trajectory tests: 4 files / 38 tests passed.\n\nOrdering coverage in `attempt-session-cleanup.test.ts`:\n\n```\nexpect(order).toEqual([flush, cleanup, session.ended, flush]);\n```\n\nTimestamp mechanism coverage in `runtime.test.ts` (fake timers, 500ms delay between `model.completed` and `session.ended`):\n\n```\nexpect(Date.parse(sessionEndedTs)).toBeGreaterThan(Date.parse(modelCompletedTs));\n```\n\nReal redacted trajectory export still pending: this machine does not have a live embedded-run setup that can produce a durable after-cleanup `session.ended` artifact. Unit/fake-timer proof remains above.\n\nData-model note: no persisted schema or event-shape migration. `session.ended` payload fields are unchanged; only emit timing moves from finalize into post-cleanup. The `runtime.test.ts` addition is fake-timer ordering coverage, not a serialized-state format change.\n\nLocal checks: `oxfmt --check` clean on touched files; `git diff --check` clean. `pnpm check:changed` could not run here (crabbox/blacksmith testbox binary unavailable on this machine).\n\n## AI-assisted\n\nYes. Authored with Cursor/Grok assistance. Human: Stan Shih (stantheman0128).",
